# Rank 1634 / CVE-2018-9918: qpdf's direct-object parser drove its
# nesting stacks without any depth ceiling, so a PDF whose object body
# is hundreds of thousands of opening brackets built a direct object
# that deep and exhausts the native stack the moment the tree is
# walked (denial of service through unbounded parse depth, CWE-400/
# CWE-674 family; qpdf issue #202). parseInternal in
# libqpdf/QPDFObjectHandle.cc is an iterative state machine over
# QPDFTokenizer tokens -- olist_stack, state_stack and offset_stack
# are pushed on every tt_array_open/tt_dict_open and popped on the
# matching close -- and the open case pushed unconditionally, so the
# depth of the parsed tree is bounded by nothing but the file. The
# fixing commit b4d6cf6836 ("Limit depth of nesting in direct objects
# (fixes #202)", naming this CVE): the open case first checks
# olist_stack.size() > 500 and, past the bound, warns about
# excessively deeply nested data and folds to null at st_top instead
# of pushing. The remediation is present at the fixed revision
# (QPDFObjectHandle.cc:1490).
#
# ATTENTION, parse nesting-depth budgets in the C++ explicit-stack
# form, held on recheck. Re-measured at the span tip (3 x --cache off
# per revision, timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB): QPDFObjectHandle.cc
# reports the same 15 findings at the fix parent and the fix (14
# VYQL-MEM-006, 1 VYQL-MEM-016, the in-function rows sitting on the
# dictionary-conversion tail and shifting only with the inserted
# guard's line offset), the full findings view and the -flags only
# view both leave the nesting push unlabelled, and the whole tree
# reports 509 findings at both revisions. The only in-loop review
# flags are IntegerSizeArithmetic on olist.size() - 1 / - 2 in the
# indirect-reference branch -- size arithmetic the vulnerable body
# already carries. The depth-ceiling vocabulary that landed since the
# first pass does not reach C++: NestedParamExpansionWithoutDepthLimit
# (ruby, with its php sibling), NestedExtglobExpansionWithoutDepthLimit
# (javascript) and the YARA ast_build_without_level_budget binding are
# each library-bound, and nothing in bindings/cpp emits
# code.UnboundedResourceOperation. The YARA control shape cannot
# transfer either: qpdf documents no nesting budget anywhere at the
# vulnerable revision (no depth or nesting constant in libqpdf/ or
# include/), so there is no documented cap for a negation to key on,
# and keying on the fix's own olist_stack.size() > 500 is the fixing
# commit's own layout. The generic shape is unshippable and is now
# measured narrower than at the first pass: across the 220 sibling
# clones, 38474 C/C++ files, 220 carry the vector-stack idiom
# (push_back beside pop_back/.back()) and 90 of those carry no size()
# or depth comparison at all; even the narrowest spelling -- while +
# switch + case + push_back + pop_back with no size()/depth comparison
# anywhere in the file -- matches 8 files, and not this one, because
# parseInternal's own body already compares olist.size() >= 2 on the
# inner vector. A control clause keyed on the generic size-comparison
# spelling is therefore satisfied at both revisions, and only the
# identifier-linked spelling discriminates. Minting a fourth
# per-shape depth sibling concept beside the three existing ones is
# the ontology-rot move the campaign rejects. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry:
# the loop, the pushes and the size comparisons all extract, so the
# missing piece is the depth-budget relation between the pushed
# container and the compared one, not a localised construct. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1634 holds three cases off
# the real code, all rejecting VYQL-DOS-029: the unbounded open case,
# the unbounded open case with the sibling-vector size guard in the
# same body (a size comparison on the inner vector is not the nesting
# budget, so it must not neutralise when depth-budget vocabulary
# lands), and the olist_stack.size()-guarded form, which must stay
# rejected.

test "rank1634: the object parser nests without a depth budget"
  lang cpp
  file libqpdf/QPDFObjectHandle.cc
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  QPDFObjectHandle
  QPDFObjectHandle::parseInternal(PointerHolder<InputSource> input,
                                  std::string const& object_description,
                                  QPDFTokenizer& tokenizer, bool& empty,
                                  StringDecrypter* decrypter, QPDF* context,
                                  bool content_stream)
  {
      empty = false;

      QPDFObjectHandle object;

      std::vector<std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle> > olist_stack;
      olist_stack.push_back(std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>());
      std::vector<parser_state_e> state_stack;
      state_stack.push_back(st_top);
      std::vector<qpdf_offset_t> offset_stack;
      qpdf_offset_t offset = input->tell();
      offset_stack.push_back(offset);
      bool done = false;
      while (! done)
      {
          std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>& olist = olist_stack.back();
          parser_state_e state = state_stack.back();
          offset = offset_stack.back();

          object = QPDFObjectHandle();

          QPDFTokenizer::Token token =
              tokenizer.readToken(input, object_description, true);

          switch (token.getType())
          {
            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_array_open:
            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_dict_open:
              olist_stack.push_back(std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>());
              state = st_start;
              offset_stack.push_back(input->tell());
              state_stack.push_back(
                  (token.getType() == QPDFTokenizer::tt_array_open) ?
                  st_array : st_dictionary);
              break;

            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_bool:
              object = newBool((token.getValue() == "true"));
              break;

            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_null:
              object = newNull();
              break;

            default:
              object = newNull();
              break;
          }

          switch (state)
          {
            case st_array:
            case st_dictionary:
              olist.push_back(object);
              break;

            case st_stop:
            {
                if ((state_stack.size() < 2) || (olist_stack.size() < 2))
                {
                    throw std::logic_error(
                        "QPDFObjectHandle::parseInternal: st_stop encountered "
                        "with insufficient stack");
                }
                parser_state_e old_state = state_stack.back();
                state_stack.pop_back();
                offset_stack.pop_back();
                if (old_state == st_array)
                {
                    object = newArray(olist);
                }
                else
                {
                    object = newDictionary(olist);
                }
                olist_stack.pop_back();
                olist_stack.back().push_back(object);
                break;
            }

            case st_top:
              done = true;
              break;

            default:
              break;
          }
      }
      return object;
  }
  ```

test "rank1634: a size guard on the inner vector is not the nesting budget"
  lang cpp
  file libqpdf/QPDFObjectHandle.cc
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  QPDFObjectHandle
  QPDFObjectHandle::parseInternal(PointerHolder<InputSource> input,
                                  std::string const& object_description,
                                  QPDFTokenizer& tokenizer, bool& empty,
                                  StringDecrypter* decrypter, QPDF* context,
                                  bool content_stream)
  {
      empty = false;

      QPDFObjectHandle object;

      std::vector<std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle> > olist_stack;
      olist_stack.push_back(std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>());
      std::vector<parser_state_e> state_stack;
      state_stack.push_back(st_top);
      std::vector<qpdf_offset_t> offset_stack;
      qpdf_offset_t offset = input->tell();
      offset_stack.push_back(offset);
      bool done = false;
      while (! done)
      {
          std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>& olist = olist_stack.back();
          parser_state_e state = state_stack.back();
          offset = offset_stack.back();

          object = QPDFObjectHandle();

          QPDFTokenizer::Token token =
              tokenizer.readToken(input, object_description, true);

          switch (token.getType())
          {
            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_array_open:
            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_dict_open:
              // The push is unbounded: the only comparison in this body
              // reads olist, the vector at the stack's top, not the
              // stack whose growth is the defect.
              olist_stack.push_back(std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>());
              state = st_start;
              offset_stack.push_back(input->tell());
              state_stack.push_back(
                  (token.getType() == QPDFTokenizer::tt_array_open) ?
                  st_array : st_dictionary);
              break;

            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_word:
            {
                std::string const& value = token.getValue();
                if ((value == "R") && (state != st_top) &&
                    (olist.size() >= 2) &&
                    (! olist.at(olist.size() - 1).isIndirect()) &&
                    (olist.at(olist.size() - 1).isInteger()) &&
                    (! olist.at(olist.size() - 2).isIndirect()) &&
                    (olist.at(olist.size() - 2).isInteger()))
                {
                    object = newIndirect(
                        context,
                        olist.at(olist.size() - 2).getIntValue(),
                        olist.at(olist.size() - 1).getIntValue());
                    olist.pop_back();
                    olist.pop_back();
                }
                else
                {
                    object = newNull();
                }
                break;
            }

            default:
              object = newNull();
              break;
          }

          switch (state)
          {
            case st_array:
            case st_dictionary:
              olist.push_back(object);
              break;

            case st_top:
              done = true;
              break;

            default:
              break;
          }
      }
      return object;
  }
  ```

test "rank1634: the fixed revision bounds the nesting depth"
  lang cpp
  file libqpdf/QPDFObjectHandle.cc
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  QPDFObjectHandle
  QPDFObjectHandle::parseInternal(PointerHolder<InputSource> input,
                                  std::string const& object_description,
                                  QPDFTokenizer& tokenizer, bool& empty,
                                  StringDecrypter* decrypter, QPDF* context,
                                  bool content_stream)
  {
      empty = false;

      QPDFObjectHandle object;

      std::vector<std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle> > olist_stack;
      olist_stack.push_back(std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>());
      std::vector<parser_state_e> state_stack;
      state_stack.push_back(st_top);
      std::vector<qpdf_offset_t> offset_stack;
      qpdf_offset_t offset = input->tell();
      offset_stack.push_back(offset);
      bool done = false;
      while (! done)
      {
          std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>& olist = olist_stack.back();
          parser_state_e state = state_stack.back();
          offset = offset_stack.back();

          object = QPDFObjectHandle();

          QPDFTokenizer::Token token =
              tokenizer.readToken(input, object_description, true);

          switch (token.getType())
          {
            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_array_open:
            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_dict_open:
              if (olist_stack.size() > 500)
              {
                  QTC::TC("qpdf", "QPDFObjectHandle too deep");
                  warn(context,
                       QPDFExc(qpdf_e_damaged_pdf, input->getName(),
                               object_description,
                               input->getLastOffset(),
                               "ignoring excessively deeply nested data structure"));
                  object = newNull();
                  state = st_top;
              }
              else
              {
                  olist_stack.push_back(std::vector<QPDFObjectHandle>());
                  state = st_start;
                  offset_stack.push_back(input->tell());
                  state_stack.push_back(
                      (token.getType() == QPDFTokenizer::tt_array_open) ?
                      st_array : st_dictionary);
              }
              break;

            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_bool:
              object = newBool((token.getValue() == "true"));
              break;

            case QPDFTokenizer::tt_null:
              object = newNull();
              break;

            default:
              object = newNull();
              break;
          }

          switch (state)
          {
            case st_array:
            case st_dictionary:
              olist.push_back(object);
              break;

            case st_stop:
            {
                if ((state_stack.size() < 2) || (olist_stack.size() < 2))
                {
                    throw std::logic_error(
                        "QPDFObjectHandle::parseInternal: st_stop encountered "
                        "with insufficient stack");
                }
                parser_state_e old_state = state_stack.back();
                state_stack.pop_back();
                offset_stack.pop_back();
                if (old_state == st_array)
                {
                    object = newArray(olist);
                }
                else
                {
                    object = newDictionary(olist);
                }
                olist_stack.pop_back();
                olist_stack.back().push_back(object);
                break;
            }

            case st_top:
              done = true;
              break;

            default:
              break;
          }
      }
      return object;
  }
  ```
